<title>USA: Chiron gets FDA clearance for ACS:Centaur.</title>
<headline>Chiron gets FDA clearance for ACS:Centaur.</headline>
<dateline>WALPOLE, Mass. 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chiron Corp said Thursday that its Chiron Diagnostics unit has received premarket notification (510K) clearance from the U.S Food and Drug Administration for its ACS:Centaur Chemiluminescent Immunoassay System.</p>
<p>The company said it expects to launch ACS: Centaur, a system designed to optimize productivity in chemical laboratories, in late 1997.</p>
